<title>LUXEMBOURG: Olive oil producers attack tree-based aid option.</title>
<headline>Olive oil producers attack tree-based aid option.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olive oil producer countries on Monday expressed strong opposition to any move to link subsidies to the number of productive trees, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Spain, backed by Portugal, Greece and Italy, would prefer to simplify the existing aid regime based on production and consumption.</p>
<p>Both options were presented in a recent report by the European Commission looking at ways to curb massive fraud.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a quick exchange of views between producers. The Farm Council will return to it in May,&quot; said an EU official, adding that experts will study new figures from the European Commission.</p>
<p>Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler warned ministers about future surpluses due to production increasing faster, especially in Spain, than consumption.</p>
<p>A bumper olive harvest was expected this year, he added.</p>
</text>
